  <related-activity ref="XM-DAC-3-1-281631" type="1"></related-activity>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved framework conditions for sustainable development</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="269605" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">SSC contributions in 2019 to framework conditions within the water sector in South Africa: &quot;4 &quot;.

Score from 1-5, 1 lowest and 5 highest.

The planned output targets in the project have been met in 2019, but there has been no progress on Water Efficiency in Industries.

2019 was marking the finalization of phase I, phase II approval and the first year of phase II implementation. Accordingly, there has been focus on detailing work plans and initiation of the relation building with new partners at the municipal level. With respect to impact, several processes and events deserves highlighting; 1) Danish dialogue based approach for environmental licencing of industries, 2) Danish approaches for sustainable ground water management in full implementation at municipal level, 3)  The Danish position on the PPP approach is being promoted and implemented at many levels, and 4) No progress on Water Efficiency in Industries track.</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2019-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="5"></target>
     <actual value="4"></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
